---
import TextSection from '../../components/TextSection.astro';
import { mailHref, site } from '../../data/facts.ts';
import { UI } from '../../data/ui.ts';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';

const locale = 'en';
const text = UI[locale];
---

<Page
  locale={locale}
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy policy – Hotel Lärchenwald"
  description="What personal data a visit to this website involves, who processes the data for us, and what rights the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection gives you."
  modified="2026-11-25"
>
  <TextSection>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We process as little personal data as possible. This policy says what data a visit to this website involves, what
      we need the data for and what rights you have. It follows the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP).
    </p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>The controller responsible for processing your personal data is:</p>
    <address>
      {site.legalName}<br>
      {site.address.street}<br>
      {site.address.postalCode}
      {site.address.locality}<br>
      {text.email}{text.colon} <a href={mailHref(site.email)}>{site.email}</a>
    </address>

    <h2>Visiting the website</h2>
    <p>
      This website is delivered through the network of Cloudflare. When you open a page, Cloudflare processes on our
      behalf the technical data that your browser sends with every request:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your IP address,</li>
      <li>the identifier of your browser and of your operating system (user agent),</li>
      <li>the address of the page that you request (URL).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cloudflare needs this data to send you the page and to protect the website against attacks. We ourselves do not
      analyse this data, and we do not link it to you as a person.
    </p>

    <h2>Processor and disclosure abroad</h2>
    <p>
      The processor is Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. The data named above can
      therefore reach the United States. This disclosure abroad rests on the Swiss-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and on
      the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, under which Cloudflare is certified.
    </p>

    <h2>Preview of new pages</h2>
    <p>
      Before we publish new pages, we check them in a protected preview. Access to it runs through Cloudflare Access:
      anyone who wants to open a preview enters an email address and receives a one-time code at that address. This
      concerns only the people whom we invite to review a page, not the visitors to this website.
    </p>

    <h2>Forms on the contact page</h2>
    <p>
      When you write to us through a form, Cloudflare Email Routing delivers your message to our mailbox. So that nobody
      misuses the forms, a counter counts the messages of each IP address for 60 seconds.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Workers Logs keep the logs of these requests for up to 7 days. They hold error codes only, never the
      content of a form.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies, statistics and display</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies and keeps no visitor statistics. We create no profiles, and we do not track which
      pages you look at.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you choose the display at the top of the page (light, dark or more contrast), your browser stores this choice
      on your device. It is not sent to us or to third parties. You can change it at any time, or delete it in the
      settings of your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You may ask us what personal data we process about you. You may ask us to correct inaccurate data, to delete data
      or to hand your data over to you in a commonly used format. To do so, write to us at
      <a href={mailHref(site.email)}>{site.email}</a>. We reply within 30 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you do not agree with our reply, you may contact the Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner
      (FDPIC) in Bern.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We adapt this policy when the website or the law changes. The version that is published here is the one that
      applies.
    </p>

    <p><small>Last updated: 25 November 2026</small></p>
  </TextSection>
</Page>
